       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Thomas Bernhart",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812",
      "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Summary of the discussion in today’s Tech Meeting:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We agreed to perform OCFL operations first. If they succeed, we execute all database operations within a single transaction. If the database transaction fails, OCFL serves as the single source of truth: after multiple failures, the transaction will roll back, and database entries will be recreated or updated by reindexing the OCFL object.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The consensus was that if OCFL operations succeed but Fedora fails to reindex the OCFL object, this likely indicates a Fedora bug: Fedora created an OCFL object on disk that it cannot read later.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Note: Fedora currently does not support reindexing an OCFL object,  which already is in the database. Only indexing OCFL object not yet present in the database is supported at the moment.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
