   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Discussed at 2025-01-30 tech meeting, needs some review of whether we could separate the database actions from the OCFL actions while allowing some handling of failures.</p>",
     "created": "30/Jan/25 12:36 PM",
     "id": "24572",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/14292/comment/24572",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "30/Jan/25 12:36 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:55ced3ed-e779-41c7-8405-264896e2b4f7",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "yuri.carrer",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A55ced3ed-e779-41c7-8405-264896e2b4f7",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Timeouts are setup to manage not responding operation, but read is responding here. So a solution can be to read the file in batches (we already use java.io.BufferedInputStream here), and at every batch we extend the timeout using the Fedora internal API on transaction timeout (by using the transaction ID). Deleting the transaction will also have the benefit to stop the long running transaction, giving the repository manager full control over it.</p>",
     "created": "03/Apr/26 7:16 AM",
     "id": "28583",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/14292/comment/28583",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "557058:55ced3ed-e779-41c7-8405-264896e2b4f7",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/73de6422ab95e3d7c4cc32c59a3962d3?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FY-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "yuri.carrer",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A55ced3ed-e779-41c7-8405-264896e2b4f7",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "03/Apr/26 7:16 AM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/16",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/24",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Thomas Bernhart",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812",
      "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
     },
     "body": "<p>Summary of the discussion in today’s Tech Meeting:</p>\n\n<p>We agreed to perform OCFL operations first. If they succeed, we execute all database operations within a single transaction. If the database transaction fails, OCFL serves as the single source of truth: after multiple failures, the transaction will roll back, and database entries will be recreated or updated by reindexing the OCFL object.</p>\n\n<p>The consensus was that if OCFL operations succeed but Fedora fails to reindex the OCFL object, this likely indicates a Fedora bug: Fedora created an OCFL object on disk that it cannot read later.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Note: Fedora currently does not support reindexing an OCFL object,  which already is in the database. Only indexing OCFL object not yet present in the database is supported at the moment.</p>",
     "created": "09/Apr/26 12:48 PM",
     "id": "28716",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/14292/comment/28716",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/16",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/24",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:6d7ce37d-04db-48cf-a4e0-23671cdcf812/be37a474-347b-42fb-8c7b-46aaace32930/32",
