  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>When creating or replacing a NonRDFSource in Fedora (<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/a2ec2ac5b273670c421b74df1ad9174b3289f663/fcrepo-http-api/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/api/FedoraLdp.java#L440C21-L440C45\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">fcrepo-http-api/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/api/FedoraLdp.java#L440C21-L440C45</a>),  the database connections needs to stay open for a long time without any activity because the binary stream (more than 100 gigabytes) is being read within the database transaction (<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/a2ec2ac5b273670c421b74df1ad9174b3289f663/fcrepo-http-api/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/api/FedoraLdp.java#L560C1-L560C48\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">fcrepo-http-api/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/api/FedoraLdp.java#L560C1-L560C48</a>). The largest files we can ingest is thus proportional to the time the database transaction can be kept open.</p>\n\n<p>A stack trace of the problem can be found here: <span class=\"nobr\"><a href=\"/rest/api/3/attachment/content/10418\" title=\"Fedora_timeout_large_file.txt attached to FCREPO-3971\" data-attachment-type=\"file\" data-attachment-name=\"Fedora_timeout_large_file.txt\" data-media-services-type=\"file\" data-media-services-id=\"d7de4591-47b1-4fb3-99ab-7f805b6042b3\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Fedora_timeout_large_file.txt<sup><img class=\"rendericon\" src=\"/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif\" height=\"7\" width=\"7\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/></sup></a></span> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Code location where the binary stream is actually read:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/AbstractNonRdfSourcePersister.java#L89\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/AbstractNonRdfSourcePersister.java#L89</a> </p>\n\n<p>Wich is called in these 2 locations:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/CreateNonRdfSourcePersister.java#L46\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/CreateNonRdfSourcePersister.java#L46</a></li>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/UpdateNonRdfSourcePersister.java#L59\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/UpdateNonRdfSourcePersister.java#L59</a></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n\n<p>Proposal: Make the database transactions shorter by fetching the binaries content outside of the transaction.</p>",
  "duedate": null,
  "environment": "Our cloud setup:<br/>\n<br/>\nFedora<br/>\n- Version: 6.5.0<br/>\n- keepaliveTime=30sec<br/>\n<br/>\nPostgres:<br/>\n- Version: 12.16<br/>\n- Custom settings: idle_in_transaction_session_timeout=180 minutes<br/>\n<br/>\nDeployed as a docker stack. The database container is in endpoint_mode: dnsrr and the port is in mode: host<br/>\n<br/>\nOur customers environments can differ and our mostly running on Windows servers.",
